Correcting the account this commit's own message gives.

The message ends with the fragment "Selected unverified. be careful", which
is editor residue rather than part of the account, and it should be read as
absent. Nothing in the change is unverified in the sense that phrase
suggests, and nothing about it warrants special care beyond the record below.

What the commit carries: the five read-request kinds declared as data, and a
dispatcher whose loop body performs the request read once and selects the
answer slots. What it does not carry, and what the message implies by
omission: a call site. Nothing in the package, the tests or the benchmarks
invokes the dispatcher, and the later program-shape census measured that it
moved no program. It was added ahead of a seam that was never wired.

That is why a subsequent change removes the dispatcher and the two request
and answer types outright rather than extending them. The declaration was
sound and the seam it anticipated did not arrive.
